II. The Story Is the Visible Solution

The system begins with unresolved tensions:

Q_0 =
\{
q_1,q_2,\ldots,q_n
\}

These may include:

* incompatible desires
* incomplete knowledge
* opposing agents
* moral constraints
* scarce resources
* hidden identities
* physical limits
* emotional needs
* narrative promises

At each moment, the system chooses an action:

a_t =
\arg\max_{a\in\mathcal A}
\Big[
U(a\mid S_t)
+
N(a\mid I)
+
E(a\mid M_t)
-
V(a\mid G)
\Big]

where:

* U = local usefulness
* N = narrative coherence
* E = emergence or generative potential
* V = invariant or governance violation

The world then updates:

S_{t+1}
=
F(S_t,a_t,\epsilon_t)

The story is the rendered trajectory:

\mathcal S
=
R(S_0,S_1,\ldots,S_T)

The audience sees a film, play, conversation, or assistant interaction.

Underneath, the system is solving itself live.

