VII. The Renderer Is Not the Kernel

The same kernel may render as:

* an AI assistant
* a live film
* a role-playing world
* a teacher
* a planning system
* an interactive ritual
* a game
* a book that rewrites itself
* a simulated civilization
* a family memory archive
* a business operating system

Formally:

R_j(\Pi)
=
P_j

Different renderers produce different experiences from the same semantic kernel.

Therefore:

\Pi \neq P_j

Pantheon should never confuse one successful rendering with the whole system.

The picture is not the painter.

The performance is not the score.

The assistant is not the kernel.

