IX. Survival Across the Journey

For the kernel to survive migration between models, people, media, or time, it must contain four forms of redundancy.

Semantic redundancy

The invariant appears in multiple representations.

I
\rightarrow
\{
\text{definition},
\text{story},
\text{equation},
\text{example},
\text{counterexample}
\}

Operational redundancy

The artifact states both what the idea means and what it does.

\text{Meaning}
+
\text{Operator}

Diagnostic redundancy

The artifact explains how to detect failure.

\text{Valid state}
+
\text{failure signature}

Reconstructive redundancy

The artifact includes enough neighboring concepts to rebuild missing pieces.

z_i
\leftrightarrow
\{
z_{i-1},z_{i+1},I,O
\}

This is not wasteful repetition.

It is semantic error correction.

