X. Fail-Forward Runtime

The system must treat error as a state transition, not merely a verdict.

After an action a_t, the result is observed:

o_t =
\operatorname{Observe}(a_t)

Error is computed:

e_t =
o_t-\widehat{o}_t

Then classified:

\operatorname{Class}(e_t)
\in
\{
\text{rendering error},
\text{operator error},
\text{model error},
\text{invariant error}
\}

Update priority:

\text{renderer}
\rightarrow
\text{operator}
\rightarrow
\text{model}
\rightarrow
\text{invariant}

Do not rewrite the soul because one costume failed.

But do not protect the invariant when reality repeatedly disproves it.

